WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.069
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.370
and writer
who you know from his work

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.773
on "Saturday Night Live,"
"The Last Man on Earth,"

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.474
and as the voice
of the Sea Captain.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:11.844
He stars in the highly
anticipated action-comedy

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.112
series "MacGruber,"

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.080
which begins streaming
on Peacock December 16th.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.182
Please welcome back to the show
my very good friend

00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:18.651
Will Forte, everybody!

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.586
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:26.225
♪♪

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:31.865
♪♪

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.467
[ Laughs ] Hi, buddy.
-Hi. How are you?

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.901
-Good. How have you recovered?

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.704
Are you doing alright?
-I went to the corner bistro

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:41.740
after that
and got a delicious burger.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.542
What I didn't know is,
I was already full

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:47.246
before I went there,
so I was like -- I couldn't --

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.415
I basically couldn't breathe
till midnight that night.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.351
We did this on Sunday.
-Yeah, well, we walked --

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.753
We had some, like,
fried chicken that was on set.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.555
And I feel like we ate a lot
of that 'cause we were so drunk

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:58.524
that we were just talking
and eating way too much chicken.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:00:59.959
-But we didn't eat the chicken

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:03.929
until 12 tequila shots in
or something like that.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.298
-So it just was floating.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.232
It wasn't even, like,
being able to be processed.

00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:08.701
-Yeah.
-I would like to say...

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:12.371
we had a lot of big, grand plans
of getting together that night.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:14.874
We were very stereotypically
drunk

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.408
because we were like,
"Let's get dinner later."

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:17.777
And you're like,
"I'll text you."

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.412
And I was like, "I'll text you."
And then we both went home

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.981
and didn't talk again
till today.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.783
-But I thought about you
the whole time.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.084
-I did, too.
-Yes.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:28.821
-Well, I -- My wife
is one of your biggest fans.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:31.658
And one of the great memories
I have of getting to be

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.493
on set for "MacGruber,"
in 2010, the film,

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:35.929
is that you shot it
in New Mexico,

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.430
as you did with the series.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.000
My wife lives -- grew up,
I should say, in New Mexico.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.701
And so we got to hang out,

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.737
you, me,
and my soon-to-be in-laws,

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.205
because we were
just dating then.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:50.243
-Yes, you guys were dating.
This was -- I don't know.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.445
I would say maybe a year
into your relationship?

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.347
-Two years. My wife --
Based on where you're going,

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.115
I want to clarify
it was two years.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:59.219
-Okay, this is two years,
which makes this story better.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.220
-Yeah, worse for me,
better to tell, yeah.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.691
-Okay, and I apologize Ariel,
your sister-in-law,

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.260
is, like, an unwilling
participant in this story.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.627
-Yeah.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:10.163
-Back in the day,
I was a single man.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.166
-Yeah.
-And Ariel was a single woman.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.933
-Yeah.
-We had, one night,

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:18.104
gone to your in-laws --
your in-laws-to-be house.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.772
And we all had a little tequila.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.708
That was another, you know,
tequila night.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.744
And, you know,
we had a little --

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.746
Ariel and I had
a little makeout session.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:27.947
-You guys made out.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.648
-Yeah. So, it was very innocent.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.651
But then we woke up
the next day.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.320
We all stayed at the house,
in separate quarters, everyone,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.021
except -- even you.

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:38.023
You were very chaste back then.

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:39.358
-I was very chaste.

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:42.028
-Anyway, we woke up,
and then we went

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.963
to this place called Bobcat.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.565
And as we were driving, Ariel
and I were in the front seat.

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:49.235
You guys, two years
into your relationship,

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.636
were into the back.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:53.906
And you had, at this point,
not yet told Alexi

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.274
that you loved her.
-I had not.

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:56.409
That is correct.
-Yeah.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:57.744
-And I did not realize,

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.979
but Ariel had told you that
when I wasn't there.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.148
So this was a piece
of information that you had

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.916
that I did not know
that you had.

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:05.985
-Yes. And I seized
upon that information.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.287
And so I made a very big deal

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:13.226
of professing my love to Ariel.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.494
-Yeah.
-In the front seat, just like,

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.663
"Ariel,
I'm just going to say it.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.532
When it's time, it's time.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.702
And, you know,
you are so special.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.004
And I just think I'm ready
to tell you right away

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.905
that I love you.

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:29.576
Any person who just feels
strongly about somebody

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.144
will tell them they love them,
and I just want to do this."

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:35.515
And you're in the back seat
going, "You son of a gun."

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.617
-And then,
I'd like to point out,

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.753
that wasn't my only terrible
heel-dragging.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.455
So, then we were together
five years,

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.724
and I still hadn't proposed.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.492
-Okay.
-And at an "SNL" --

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.362
I was at an "SNL" after party.
You'd left "SNL."

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.531
And I was at "SNL."
-Screw that place!

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.132
Who needs it, right?!
-I know.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.633
I didn't want you
to get into all that.

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:57.035
-Best job ever.
Would not be here without it.

00:03:57.035 --> 00:03:59.238
I love you, Lorne.
I love everything about it.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:00.973
-Alright.
So, I'm at a table,

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.775
at the after party,
with Alexi and Ariel again.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:03.842
-Yeah.
-And you walk in.

00:04:03.842 --> 00:04:05.278
I didn't even know
you were coming.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:09.348
You see us.
Beeline over, take a knee.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:11.483
-[ Laughter ]
-I forgot this!

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:13.519
-Take a knee to Ariel,
and you're like,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.820
"I want to say something

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.524
that I have waited
way too long to say.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.893
Ariel, I love you.
Will you marry me?"

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:24.897
And I was like, "You mother..."
Twice!

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.832
-Well, you're married now
with three kids, right?

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:28.034
-With three kids, yeah.

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.335
-And I'd like to think
that I have a little

00:04:30.335 --> 00:04:33.172
part of that action.
That's a weird way to say that.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.741
-You do have a part
of that action.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.208
-Yeah.

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:37.944
It's all about action to me
and being a part of the action.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.346
You're either a part
of the action or you're not.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.782
Yeah.
-You -- This is so exciting.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:46.585
So, this was a sketch, a beloved
sketch that became a movie

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:48.754
that I think we can be honest
about the fact

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.723
that is beloved now.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.359
People who have discovered
the film in the last 10 years.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.960
-Thank you for saying that.
-Yeah.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.229
-Yeah.
-We all know --

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.699
-It was not --
It was not beloved at the time.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:02.401
Or maybe -- You know, maybe
the people who saw it liked it.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:03.603
-I think they did.

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.837
-But definitely not a lot
of people saw it.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.305
We can agree on that for sure.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.640
-Yes, let's just drill down
and say, like, box office-wise

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.142
it did not set the world
on fire.

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:12.244
-[Bleep] the bed.

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:14.447
Just like --
I mean, the bed was --

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:18.551
At the end of that
was more [bleep] than bed.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.720
Yeah.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.723
-So it's very exciting
for the fans of this

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.291
that it's now not just back,

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.526
it's not a sequel,
it's a new series.

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:29.062
It's eight episodes.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:30.763
What I've seen of it
is so exciting,

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.165
being a huge fan of the film.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.666
Did you always --
In the back of your head,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.335
did you and Jorma
and John Solomon

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:37.669
think like, "You know what?

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:39.472
Maybe one day,
we'll make more of these"?

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:43.042
-We pretty immediately after --
You know,

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.544
when the dust settled in our
head after a couple of weeks,

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:48.414
it's hard to go through
a situation like that.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.082
But early on, we said,
"You know what?

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:51.651
We're proud of this thing.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:54.053
Nobody wants a sequel,
but let's give them one.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.089
Let's just frickin' do it."

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:58.825
And we were like, "Even if we
have to shoot it on iPhones,

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.526
let's just -- let's do it."

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:03.596
So we immediately started
thinking of titles.

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.297
We came up with
the dumbest titles.

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:07.400
-What were some
of the rejected --

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.770
-"MacGruber 2:
[Bleep] Infested Waters."

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.604
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.604 --> 00:06:14.874
Another one --
Jorma, I think, had

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:20.146
"Hawaiian Gold: MacGruber 2:
The Search for Hawaiian Gold."

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.081
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:26.319
Val Kilmer had --
He had a simple one.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:27.487
"MacTwober."

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:28.821
-"MacTwober."
-Yeah.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.022
And then Wiig, I think, said

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.959
"MacGruber Part Deux Part --"
Wait.

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:35.727
"MacGruber Part Deux, Deux."

00:06:35.727 --> 00:06:37.630
Just so it could get
"doo-doo" in there.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.965
-I also -- Yeah, somebody
pitched at the time

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:42.134
"MacGruber Goes Number 2"
as a sequel title.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:43.335
-Oh, that was Wiig also.

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:44.903
-Yeah, that was a really
good one, as well.

00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:46.972
This is very exciting.
We're going to show a clip of it

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:49.442
and then talk more about it
when we come back with more

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.244
from Will Forte after this.

